cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this skill in academic work, cite the software release and the specific manifest/snapshot identity, not the documentation revision alone."
title: "admet-screening: auditable ADMET decision support"
type: software
version: "0.9.0"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "admet-screening contributors"
abstract: >-
  A layered ADMET decision-support skill with identity/unit normalization,
  source-level admission, abstention, long-table data contracts, and
  reproducibility/evidence gates. Capability level is 4.0-dev; it is not a
  validated ADMET predictor and must not be cited as such.
keywords:
  - ADMET
  - cheminformatics
  - applicability domain
  - abstention
  - reproducibility
